# Hashed artifacts must survive checkout byte-for-byte.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf enabled, so git would otherwise
# rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout. For the frozen splits that is fatal: the bytes would
# change, `sha256sum -c splits.sha256` would fail on a fresh clone, and the benchmark would
# appear tampered with. `-text` disables all newline translation for these paths.
benchmark/splits/** -text

# Fixtures are compared byte-wise by the test suite for the same reason.
src/ecopulse_ca/ingest/fixtures/*.json -text

# Everything else may follow the platform default.
* text=auto
